    "q-340778": {
      "dom_id": "step-q340778",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of a function from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above.  What is the constant Fourier coefficient of  $f(x)+1?$",
      "worked_solution": "The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nRecall that if $C$ is a constant, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $f(x)+C$ are\n\n- ${a}_{0}+2C$  for the constant coefficient,\n\n- ${a}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- ${b}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nIn our case, $C=1.$ Therefore, the constant Fourier coefficient of $f(x)+1$ is ${a}_{0}+2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-340778-a",
