    "q-340781": {
      "dom_id": "step-q340781",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of a function from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $7$th sine Fourier coefficient of $f(-x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nRecall that the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $f(-x)$ are\n\n- ${a}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- ${a}_{n}$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $-{b}_{n}$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $7$th sine coefficient of $f(-x)$ is $-{b}_{7}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
